{
  "id": "08510_soretonaku",
  "headword": "それとなく",
  "reading": "それとなく",
  "part_of_speech": "adverb",
  "gloss": "indirectly; casually; subtly",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "indirectly; casually; subtly",
      "explanation": "describes doing something in a way that is not direct or obvious, often to avoid being noticed or to be tactful"
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "08510_soretonaku_ex1",
      "japanese": "それとなく{聞|き}いてみた。",
      "english": "I casually asked about it.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "08510_soretonaku_ex2",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}にそれとなく{伝|つた}えた。",
      "english": "I subtly conveyed it to him.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "08510_soretonaku_ex3",
      "japanese": "それとなく{様子|ようす}を{探|さぐ}ってみた。",
      "english": "I tried to discreetly find out what was going on.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "08510_soretonaku_ex4",
      "japanese": "{母|はは}はそれとなく{結婚|けっこん}の{話|はなし}を{持|も}ち{出|だ}した。",
      "english": "My mother casually brought up the topic of marriage.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed when doing something indirectly or subtly to avoid being too obvious or direct. Common in situations requiring tact or discretion.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- それとなく{聞|き}く - to ask casually\n- それとなく{伝|つた}える - to convey indirectly\n- それとなく{探|さぐ}る - to probe subtly\n- それとなく{示|しめ}す - to hint at\n\nRELATED:\n- {遠回|とおまわ}しに - in a roundabout way\n- {暗|あん}に - implicitly\n- さりげなく - nonchalantly",
